two years ago some unhappy t1 fans sent  a truck to their team's headquarters  with messages on it lambasting the org  for what they felt was a gross  mismanagement of the team at the time  recently this past week they've started  doing it again and all of this comes at  a time when t1 have been asking fans  even those with good intentions to  please stay away from players houses  it's another bizarre t1 story let's get  into it  all right then just before we talk about  t1 it's time to remind you guys that we  are so  excruciatingly close to two million  subscribers if you're watching this and  you've thought about subscribing but  you've never quite got around to it  please consider subscribing we are so  close now and you could help us get  there thanks okay so a few weeks ago i  shared the news that faker was suing  some of his toxic fans leaving him  malicious images and comments online on  july 19th faker's legal team apex law  spoke to press in south korea to  announce they had filed a lawsuit  against those who have written malicious  comments against faker online faker's  lawyers described the content he'd been  sent as unspeakably foul but in the past  t1 has been subjected to behavior which  can be better categorized as just weird  in that video i touched on one famous  example of this there was an incident in  which some t1 fans circled around the  headquarters of skt the parent company  of t1 to protest among other things the  potential hiring of new team management  the message board on their truck  lambasted t1 for hiring famed league  coach and personality ls who they  described as a coach who would cause  public controversy at the time this  specific stunt felt like a bit of a  one-off we've seen fans in korea do some  pretty strange things when criticizing  their teams especially t1 fans but  nothing quite like this well last week i  definitely wondered if people had been  digging up old pictures from that event  when i saw images being circulated that  looked extremely similar to the ones  from 2020 but no it's happened again on  august 4th angry t1 fans once again  hired an led truck to protest about t1's  coaching staff this time it stood in  front of the t1 building and then moved  on towards lol park the theater where  the regular season lck games are played  ahead of t1's match against hanwha live  esports this is the truck outside lol  park people take pictures of it  i don't know what it says  the truck is just parked on the road  outside lol park i guess it's in here  invent global translated the various  images on display one red incompetent  head coach relegation team coach  admitted lack of ability the solution is  to sign a coach that has experienced  winning worlds the seven years of glory  made by skt fans leave from three years  of incompetence another message said  appoint a high-level former player  coaching staff that the t1 players  deserve performance going backward  unqualified coaches who don't even  prepare for matches we've had enough  there was also players spend time  analyzing the other team while coaches  play friendly games when the league is  in progress who is the coach and finally  we don't need an incompetent coaching  staff that doesn't even know the draft  sign proven former player coaches now  clearly this is all a bit vague if  you're only just learning about it so  what exactly are these fans unhappy  about with t1's coaches well last month  t1's largest korean fan community shared  an open letter to t1 on a site called dc  inside which is not too dissimilar to  reddit and part of it was aimed  specifically at moment one of the team's  coaches they criticized him for having  only previously played and coached in  lower divisions including a quote  dishonorable demotion as coach of jin  air green wings where the team finished  their 29 season with a famous one win  and 35 loss record discussing more  recent events the letter addressed t1's  loss to rng at msi 2022 finals they  described his pick and ban strategy as  quote advantage donating and that not  only did he let down two million fans in  the process but that his pick and ban  strategy's instability has not improved  since then honestly i could keep going  here large portions of this open letter  were dedicated to just ripping into  moment demanding he answers their  questions and suggesting that he's  incapable of getting them to worlds this  year head coach polt didn't escape  criticism either of course in this  letter paul has been catching flack from  some t1 fans since he was hired back in  2020. in fact he was a sizeable part of  the reason that unhappy t1 fans sent the  original truck to the skt headquarters  the first time the t1 head coach was  once a starcraft 2 pro back in the day  before moving into the world of team  fight tactics clearly this guy knows  strategy but some t1 fans couldn't  accept a coach with little to no  experience in league of legends and to  be honest they haven't really got off  his back about it since despite the  team's resurgence over the past year  that he has directly overseen one word  you'll notice that comes up a lot in  criticism of t1's coaching staff by fans  is worlds it's a really big deal for  them now some of you guys may already  know i'm a tsm fan and honestly these  days i'm happy to just even make  playoffs i don't have a very high bar at  all at the moment but for t1 fans it's a  bit different with three worlds titles  and two msi titles under their belt t1  fans have rightly or wrongly come to  expect a different pedigree from their  team granted it's been a fair few years  since they won either of those  tournaments but no team has been able to  surpass their international trophy  counts since and t1 fans would like to  keep it that way the monstrous  record-breaking spring split they just  had hasn't been enough to keep the  critics at bay faker and his four  extremely talented young team-mates  should have been able to silence any  haters after not losing a single series  to any other korean team for the first  half of 2022 many teams would be happy  with that but it just ain't worlds i  guess so the first time these t1 fans  sent these message boards was back in  2020 the second time was on august 4th  and then as i was looking into that it  happened again on august 7th the trucks  had similar messages to before as  translated by inven global this one read  there's no need for incompetent coaches  that don't even know how to draft  appoint former player coaches that have  already proven themselves performers  going backward unqualified coaches who  don't even prepare for matches we've had  enough at this point i just want to  remind everyone that t1 are currently 14  and 2 in the lck in fact those two  losses are the only domestic lck losses  they've had all year so far they've  definitely not looked as dominant as  they were in spring but yeah i think  that's an important piece of context to  keep in mind another message read  scarecrow head coach polt  sabotaging moment take responsibility  and resign another said incompetent head  coach relegation team coach admitted  lack of ability the solution is to sign  a coach that has experienced winning  worlds the seven years of glory made by  skt fans leave from three years of  incompetence the notion of hiring  coaches that specifically have  experience of winning worlds is  something that comes up a lot in these  stunts and open letters to t1 t1 ceo joe  marsh addressed this directly last week  saying 100 fans wasted money on a truck  they don't speak for the other 1 million  fans you failed to mention we had  world's winning coaches in 2020 and 2021  one didn't make worlds and the other was  replaced mid-season just thought the  full context would be helpful to the  readers like i touched on before  demanding a coach that has literally  taken home the greatest trophy league of  legends has to offer might seem a little  crazy to 